# Tests

```rocci
@test helloNamePresent = Bool.true

@test{fixture: helloSample}
helloFixturePaired = Str.contains(helloSample.name, "Ada")
```

`@test` is a root-only declaration. The name is a Roc identifier. The right-hand
side is a boolean Roc expression. Optional `{fixture: ident}` names a local
`@fixture` binding so the expression can use that sample.

`rocci build` does **not** emit `expect` into generated Roc. `rocci test`
stages a type module plus an `expect` trailer and runs `roc test` on that
file. Files with no `@test` exit 0.

`@test` is invalid in Rocdown documents.

**Errors:** `@test` inside a component body; unknown `fixture` name; unknown
attribute; missing name or `=`.

**Related:** [Fixtures](/docs/reference/language/fixtures/),
[CLI test](/docs/reference/cli/#test).
